.TH CLAIM-DRIFT 1 "2026-08-18" "realisateur" "bashified verb"
.SH NAME
claim-drift \- has a pull request grown since it was presented as done?
.SH SYNOPSIS
.\" bashify: norun -- reaches GitHub
.B claim-drift
.I pr-number
...
.br
.\" bashify: norun -- reaches GitHub
.B claim-drift
--all
.br
.\" bashify: norun -- reaches GitHub
.B claim-drift
--strict
.I ...
.br
.\" bashify: norun -- reaches GitHub
.B claim-drift
--repo
.I owner/name
.SH DESCRIPTION
A pull request is described once, when it is opened, and then keeps
changing. This compares what a PR now contains against the claim its body
makes, and reports the gap.
.PP
It is a DIFF test and nothing more. It cannot see the conversation, so it
cannot judge whether a
.B DECISION:
line was warranted \(em a check that tried was deleted, having failed to
flag the very pull request that introduced it, twice.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --all
Audit every open pull request instead of named ones.
.TP
.B --strict
Exit nonzero on drift instead of only reporting it.
.TP
.BI --repo " owner/name"
Default is the remote of the current checkout.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Audited; either no --strict, or --strict and nothing drifted.
.TP
.B 1
--strict, and at least one PR has grown since it was claimed done.
.TP
.B 6
BLIND \(em the tracker could not be read. A domain that existed and was NOT
read is never a pass.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR closeout-lint (1)
